{
  "name": "symbols_batch",
  "description": "USE WHEN: you need source (+ optionally direct callers/callees) for several EXACT qualified_names in one round trip — e.g. following up on a locate/search result list. Requires exact qualified_name, not a bare symbol name: an id that doesn't match exactly comes back found:false instead of fuzzy-substituting the closest name (unlike understand's fuzzy search). NOT FOR: a single bare-name lookup (use source/symbol_info) or exploring an unknown name (use search/locate first to get exact qualified_names). Capped at 50 ids per call.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "required": [
      "qualified_names"
    ],
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "qualified_names": {
        "description": "Exact `qualified_name`s to fetch (e.g. `path/to/file.rs::Type::method`)\n— NOT bare names. Get these from a prior `search`/`locate` call. This\ntool does no fuzzy matching: an id that doesn't match exactly comes\nback `found: false` for that entry rather than silently substituting\nthe closest name. Capped at 50 entries per call (extras are dropped,\nsee `truncated`).",
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "include_callers": {
        "description": "`true` to also include each found symbol's direct callers (same\nshape as `callers`'s `direct` field — no transitive/ambiguous split).",
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false
      },
      "include_callees": {
        "description": "`true` to also include each found symbol's direct callees.",
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false
      },
      "lean": {
        "description": "`true` to skip computing `preview` text for each `direct_callers`/\n`direct_callees` entry — symbol identity, `line`, `edge_kind`, and\n`edge_confidence` are still returned, just not the disk-read\ncall-site snippet. Cuts both the I/O cost of reading each distinct\ncall-site file (`line_previews_batched`) and the response's byte\nsize (an omitted `preview` is dropped from the JSON entirely, not\nsent as `null`) — useful when only counting/listing callers across\na large batch, not reading the code around each call site. Ignored\nwhen neither `include_callers` nor `include_callees` is set.",
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false
      }
    }
  },
  "outputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "$defs": {
      "ErrorDetail": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "recoverable": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "review": {
            "description": "Set only on HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW / DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH — everything needed to relay-approve/decline via review_decide_via_agent_relay.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/PendingReviewPacket"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "next_call": {
            "description": "The exact next tool call this error implies, if unambiguous — same shape as suggested_next.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code",
          "message",
          "recoverable"
        ]
      },
      "PendingReviewPacket": {
        "description": "Wave 3 (audit follow-up, 2026-08-23): the structured shape of a\n`HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW`/`DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH` error's\n`review` field -- lets a calling agent relay-approve/decline without\never reading `pending_reviews` directly or reimplementing\n`hash_content` itself.\n\nWave 14 (audit follow-up, 2026-08-24): `diff_digest` is NOT\n`hash_content` of THIS packet's own `diff_preview` field -- it's\n`hash_content` of the full, unsanitized, uncapped diff stored server-\nside (see `from_pending`'s own comment). It exists to prove identity/\nfreshness (\"this is really the review you fetched, not a stale or\nguessed copy\"), not to let a caller verify \"the text I'm looking at\nhashes to this\" -- that's structurally impossible to guarantee anyway,\nsince different surfaces (this JSON packet vs. `calm review show`'s\nterminal output) apply different sanitize/cap transforms to the same\nunderlying diff and can't all match one digest. Callers must always\nCOPY this value verbatim, never recompute it from `diff_preview`.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "review_id": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "diff_preview": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "preview_truncated": {
            "description": "`true` when `diff_preview` was cut down from the full diff\n`diff_digest` covers -- see the struct's own doc comment.",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "diff_digest": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "expires_at": {
            "type": "number",
            "format": "double"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "review_id",
          "diff_preview",
          "preview_truncated",
          "diff_digest",
          "expires_at"
        ]
      },
      "SuggestedNext": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "tool": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "args": true,
          "gate": {
            "description": "true iff skipping `tool` is hook-enforced, not just advisory.",
            "type": [
              "boolean",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "required_user_input": {
            "description": "Names any `tool` param intentionally left out of `args` because only a human can safely supply it (e.g. `approve`). Absent means `args` is already complete.",
            "type": [
              "array",
              "null"
            ],
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "tool",
          "reason"
        ]
      },
      "SymbolsBatchEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "qualified_name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "found": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "kind": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "path": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "line_start": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "line_end": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "language": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "is_hub": {
            "type": [
              "boolean",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "source": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "token_estimate": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "content_warning": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "direct_callers": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CallerEntry"
            }
          },
          "direct_callees": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CalleeEntry"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "qualified_name",
          "found"
        ]
      },
      "CallerEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "symbol": {
            "description": "`path::name` (or `path::Class::name`) of the calling symbol — split on the first `::` for the file path standalone.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "edge_confidence": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "formal_source": {
            "description": "Source behind edge_confidence == \"formal\": \"stack_graphs\" | \"scip\" | \"lsp\". None when edge_confidence != \"formal\". See ADR-0002 — not equally trustworthy.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "edge_kind": {
            "description": "\"call\" or \"reference\" (e.g. a SQL JOIN reading a table) — see call_edges.edge_kind.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "preview": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "symbol",
          "edge_confidence",
          "edge_kind"
        ]
      },
      "CalleeEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "symbol": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "path": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "edge_confidence": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "formal_source": {
            "description": "See `CallerEntry::formal_source`.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "edge_kind": {
            "description": "See `CallerEntry::edge_kind`.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "preview": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "symbol",
          "path",
          "edge_confidence",
          "edge_kind"
        ]
      },
      "Caveat": {
        "description": "Structured, machine-checkable hint attached to a tool result whose\nliteral content (empty list / not-found) could otherwise be misread as\nproof of absence. `class` lets a safety gate branch without parsing\n`message`; `message` is the human-readable explanation. Design mirrors\nzzet/gortex's `ZeroEdgeCaveat` (Apache-2.0) — reimplemented against\nCALM's own resolver shape, not a line-for-line port.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "class": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "class",
          "message"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "flow_state"
    ],
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "flow_state": {
        "description": "Wave 11 (item 3, \"unified continuation state machine\"): present on\nevery response regardless of success/error -- `\"ready\"` on success,\nor one of `needs_context`/`needs_human_review`/`needs_verification`/\n`blocked` on error (see `classify_error_state`'s own doc comment).\nLets an agent dispatch on ONE top-level field instead of\nmaintaining its own per-`code` remediation table across ~70\ndistinct codes.\n\nNamed `flow_state`, not the more obvious `state` (audit follow-up,\n2026-08-23): several tool-specific success structs (e.g.\n`EditTransactionStatusOutput`, `VerifyChangeOutput` in txn.rs) have\ntheir own unrelated `state` field, and this struct's `success: T` is\n`#[serde(flatten)]`ed -- a same-named field there would silently\nserialize as a SECOND `\"state\"` JSON key (serde's flatten writes\neach field independently; nothing dedupes it), with most JSON\nparsers then last-write-wins-ing over whichever value serialized\nsecond. `flow_state` is deliberately namespaced so no domain output\nstruct will ever pick the same name by coincidence again.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "error": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ErrorDetail"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "results": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SymbolsBatchEntry"
        }
      },
      "found_count": {
        "type": "integer",
        "format": "uint",
        "minimum": 0
      },
      "not_found_count": {
        "type": "integer",
        "format": "uint",
        "minimum": 0
      },
      "truncated": {
        "description": "`true` when more than `SYMBOLS_BATCH_MAX` distinct ids were\nrequested — only the first `SYMBOLS_BATCH_MAX` (input order, after\ndedup) were looked up.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "caveat": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Caveat"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "suggested_next": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "annotations": {
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false
  }
}
